@startuml
title Weekly scheduler and serialized rebuild queue — v4

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber

participant "Cloudflare Cron\n0 3 * * SUN (Sun 03:00 UTC)" as Cron
control "Worker\nscheduled handler" as Scheduler
queue "Cloudflare Queue\nmax_batch_size=1\nmax_concurrency=1\nretry_delay=30s" as Queue
control "Queue Consumer" as Consumer
database "D1" as D1
participant "Spotify" as Spotify

== Owner-triggered start ==

actor Owner
Owner -> Scheduler: POST /api/owner/refresh\n(owner session + same-origin CSRF)
alt No active job, or previous job failed systemically
  Scheduler -> D1: Create a fresh generation in preflight
  Scheduler -> Queue: Send {generation, revision: 0} immediately
else Legacy quota or exhausted upstream failure
  Scheduler -> D1: Reactivate the same generation and cursors\nwithout deleting staging; preserve the retry deadline
  Scheduler -> Queue: Send the recovered generation + new revision
else Active or cooling-down job
  Scheduler -> Queue: Re-send the same generation + revision;\nwake immediately for database-only publication during\ndiscovery waits, otherwise use the remaining gate delay
  Scheduler --> Owner: Return current status (no duplicate job)
end

== Sunday 03:00 UTC tick ==

Cron -> Scheduler: scheduled event
Scheduler -> D1: Read the singleton rebuild_jobs row

alt No job (idle)
  Scheduler -> D1: Create generation "v4-…" phase=preflight\nrevision=0
  Scheduler -> Queue: Send {generation, revision: 0} immediately
  Scheduler -> D1: Persist next_refresh_at =\nnext Sunday 03:00 UTC
else Active job with a retry cooldown
  Scheduler -> Queue: Re-send current {generation, revision}\nwith the remaining cooldown as delay
  note right of Scheduler
    Wakes a sleeping rebuild. A second tick never
    starts an overlapping rebuild: the singleton job
    row is the serialization point.
  end note
else Legacy transient failure
  Scheduler -> D1: Resume the same generation and all saved work
  Scheduler -> Queue: Send the recovered revision with its remaining delay
else Systemically failed job
  Scheduler -> D1: Purge the failed job, its staging,\nand its work queues
  Scheduler -> D1: Create a fresh generation (preflight)
  Scheduler -> Queue: Send the new generation immediately
end

== Every 15 minutes: stalled-work watchdog ==

Cron -> Scheduler: */15 * * * * scheduled event
Scheduler -> D1: Read active job and durable gates
alt Active and overdue by at least two minutes\nafter update, lease, pacing and retry deadlines
  Scheduler -> Queue: Re-send current {generation, revision}
else Idle, failed, working or cooling down
  Scheduler -> Scheduler: No action; keep weekly schedule
end

== One serialized unit of work per delivery ==

loop One delivery at a time
  Queue -> Consumer: {generation, revision}
  Consumer -> D1: Read the current job

  alt Missing or different generation
    Consumer -> Queue: ACK stale delivery
  else Stale revision
    Consumer -> Queue: ACK stale delivery (no cursor regression)
  else A dispatch is still pending
    Consumer -> Queue: Re-send the current revision
    Consumer -> Queue: ACK this delivery
  else Spotify retry/pacing deadline is still in the future
    Consumer -> D1: After initial exclusions are frozen, find up to 30\nalready validated unpublished recordings for one artist
    alt Eligible staging and lease acquired
      Consumer -> D1: Atomic publication + counts + separate publication cursor;\npreserve source cursors, revision and all provider deadlines
      Consumer -> Queue: Send the same revision immediately for more database work
    else No eligible staging or lease held elsewhere
      Consumer -> Queue: Re-send after the remaining durable gate delay
    end
    Consumer -> Queue: ACK this delivery (no Spotify requests)
  else Another consumer holds the lease
    Consumer -> Queue: Retry the delivery later (no overlap)
  else Current work item
    Consumer -> D1: Acquire the refresh lease
    Consumer -> Consumer: Honor the pacing clock:\nadaptive gap: pages start at 2s,\n30 track requests wait ≥30s\n(durable next_read_at) and any retry_at cooldown
    Consumer -> Spotify: At most one Spotify page this unit
    Spotify --> Consumer: Page or failure
    Consumer -> D1: Persist results, release lease,\nincrement revision, set dispatch_pending
    Consumer -> Queue: Send the next revision with a delay\n(2s for a page, 30s for 30 track reads)
    Consumer -> D1: Clear dispatch_pending
    Consumer -> Queue: ACK this delivery
  end
end

note over Queue,Consumer #FFF2CC
  The consumer is deliberately serialized (one message,
  one batch, one concurrency), so exactly one rebuild
  generation progresses at a time and the D1 lease is a
  second guard, not the only one.
end note

note over Consumer,Spotify #FFDDDD
  Failures are classified per unit:
  · rolling 429 → honor Retry-After, delayed re-send,
    no retry attempt consumed; double pacing multiplier\n    and reduce metadata concurrency/batch size
  · QUOTA_EXCEEDED 429 → save progress and pause; retry
    at valid Retry-After, otherwise back off 15m to 6h.
    One-request metadata probe, no upstream attempt consumed.
    Keep the same generation, cursors, and staged tracks.
    Re-send long waits in chunks of at most 12h; every
    delivery checks the full durable retry_at deadline.
    Chunks stay below the queue’s 24h retention window.
  · 5xx → persisted exponential backoff 30s/60s/…,
    after 5 attempts pause for 1h, then resume the same work
  · other 4xx → systemic fail (bad request class)
  A systemic fail keeps the live shelf untouched and the
  failed job row in place for the next Sunday tick to
  replace. See flow 04 for the crawl phases.
end note

@enduml
